  "body": "From https://html.spec.whatwg.org/multipage/embedded-content.html#dimension-attributes:\n\n> The two attributes **[ed: width and height]** must be omitted if the resource in question does not have both an intrinsic width and an intrinsic height.\n\nThis makes absolutely no sense.  What possible reason is there for it to be author-level invalid to specify `<img width=50 height=100 src=stretchy-image.svg>`?  If anything, that's the one case where width and height are _required_ to get a sensible result; without them, an SVG with no dimensions sizes itself to 300x150.\n\nUnless there's a great reason that I'm completely missing for this, this sentence should just be dropped.\n",
